From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: hwmon: qcom-bcl: reject empty PM7550BA current samples

The exact OEM driver treats a zero PM7550BA current ADC sample as
unavailable and retains its previous reading. Return ENODATA without
renewing the cache instead of publishing a false fresh zero. Keep other
PMIC descriptors unchanged.

--- a/drivers/hwmon/qcom-bcl-hwmon.c
+++ b/drivers/hwmon/qcom-bcl-hwmon.c
@@ -906,6 +906,10 @@
 	 * Current ADC reading is in 2's complement form.
 	 * Sign extend the value based on data field bit size.
 	 */
+	/* PM7550BA can return an empty sample; it does not prove zero current. */
+	if (desc == &pm7550ba_data && !raw_val)
+		return -ENODATA;
+
 	signed_val = sign_extend32(raw_val, desc->data_field_bits_size - 1);
 
 	bcl->last_curr_input =
